A||||6||JSocha||1986 GT  --> Rear Window Defog conversion question...||||5||
Z||000000||JSocha||09-27-2001||10:28 AM||||First, thank you to those regarding my compression level questions yesterday!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I feel more comfortable now.<P>Next, since my 86 GT is at the mechanics and I can not check at the moment for wiring at the dash panel, thought I would get the question going and hopefully get an answer here today.<P>The 86 I picked up, did not have the rear window defog/defrost option added.<P>Wondering:  Is the wiring harness already there to add the switch at the dash panel as well as to add the glass with the defrost wires?<P>I may consider upgrading the back window for my daughter if I can add it because of ND winter's and the ability for her to see out the back window, especially if the side windows and mirrors are frosted up.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||09-27-2001||12:02 PM||||As far as I know the wiring harness is not there. I put a rear window defroster in my son's 88GT and I had to swipe the wiring harness and timer unit from a donor car.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rick 88||09-27-2001||05:31 PM||||Replacing the window itself is the tough part. You might want to farm this out to the pros. The wiring, switch and timer will have to be installed. Some people say the engine heat is enough to keep the window clear. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||JetroGT||09-27-2001||06:00 PM||||You need to remove the rear clip to get to the rear window. It's not hard, just time consuming. Vertical windows don't collect frost as fast as the other ones do. Don't ask me why.||||reg||1
Z||000004||JSocha||09-27-2001||06:26 PM||||My '87 GT back window frosted up in the winter the few times I did drive it.  Good thing for the rear window defrost option.  Hence the reason I was thinking, if it is possible, of having that window swaped out by professionals.<P>However, if the exsisting wiring harness on the 86 does not have the connectors for the glass as well as the switch and I would subsequently have to add it to get that functionality, I will just scratcth that idea all together and my daughter can use an ice scraper or become a better driver in the winter.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Just wanted to know if the harness was pre-setup for it already, but it sounds like it is not, unless somebody tells me differently.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||09-27-2001||07:26 PM||||That window is just nasty to work on.<P>Note, the various books say the timer is 10 minutes first cycle and 5 each time after untill you start the car again. There is another time... It's 5 and 2.5 minutes respectivly. So don't automatically think your timer is bad because it won run 10 and 5.... ((The timer label even says the timing values on it.))<P>I don't know how much you have to tear things apart to hook it up... The C200 terminal block shown in the manuals is on the side up under the left speaker. The only way to reach it is pull the speaker. (Assuming you don't have to pull the whole dash to do this one...)<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fierowrecker||09-27-2001||07:34 PM||||Hey JSocha!<BR>Do yourself and your daughter a favor...<BR>Get a winter beater, and store the Fiero...<BR>I drove my first Fiero 13 years summer and winter, now it is a rust bucket and unsafe to drive...<BR>Not to mention the poor handling characteristics of a Fiero on snow and ice...<BR>As far as frost, I hardly ever had any problems on the rear glass, but the wind shield sure ices up bad!<P><P>------------------<BR>crash... The Fierowrecker<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/crash_sig.jpg">        <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||1
